{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/843641-2e-infernals-3e-abyssals","id":843641,"title":"2e Infernals & 3e Abyssals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-07T15:37:59-08:00","id":843641,"title":"2e Infernals & 3e Abyssals","content":"Do you guys think that Abyssals will be able to fashion themselves into custom Deathlords the same way Infernals made themselves into Devil-Tigers? Or would that be too samey?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T15:52:38-08:00","id":843649,"title":"","content":"Maybe, if their relationship really is master and apprentice as stated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T16:13:35-08:00","id":843660,"title":"","content":"I doubt it. Doesn't seem like very interesting design territory, anyway, since you can basically become a Deathlord by kicking one off their throne or carving out your own black empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T16:29:04-08:00","id":843669,"title":"","content":"Are you saying that Abyssals should be tied to Deathlords that tightly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T17:07:36-08:00","id":843691,"title":"","content":"If an abyssal wants to be an uberghost, they need to kill themselves and become a old powerful uberghost through time and hard work. I'd much rather kick my deathord off it's throne and forge it into the soulsteel crown I wear on my head while I rule it's former domain while I live as a deathknight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T17:14:22-08:00","id":843696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/843641-2e-infernals-3e-abyssals?p=843691#post843691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an abyssal wants to be an uberghost, they need to kill themselves and become a old powerful uberghost through time and hard work. I'd much rather kick my deathord off it's throne and forge it into the soulsteel crown I wear on my head while I rule it's former domain while I live as a deathknight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily required in this edition, I'd wager. The deathlords might be more about enabling Abyssals in order to make the Underworld more vibrant, to give some greater weight to the passion plays and what would otherwise be empty, endless back and forths of conquest and retreat over the ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T17:50:34-08:00","id":843710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/843641-2e-infernals-3e-abyssals?p=843691#post843691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an abyssal wants to be an uberghost, they need to kill themselves and become a old powerful uberghost through time and hard work. I'd much rather kick my deathord off it's throne and forge it into the soulsteel crown I wear on my head while I rule it's former domain while I live as a deathknight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mean actually BECOMING a Deathlord, but rather creating charms based on your own interpretation of the void's deathly essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T17:57:25-08:00","id":843713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/843641-2e-infernals-3e-abyssals?p=843710#post843710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mean actually BECOMING a Deathlord, but rather creating charms based on your own interpretation of the void's deathly essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't those just be custom (and possibly esoteric) Abyssal charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T17:59:01-08:00","id":843714,"title":"","content":"We know that Infernals won't get Devil Tiger in this edition, so I doubt Abyssals will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T18:46:49-08:00","id":843727,"title":"","content":"I think the idea that Deathlords are some blatently other category of being like some ghetto ghost akuma is probably not going to be something talked about or stated as their nature. Deathlords are still powerful ghosts, but that power likely comes from centuries of building infrastructure and wresting the powers of the Labyrinth to their will.<br /> <br /> So Abyssals likely can replace them, but it won't be some checklist of metaphysical powers that an Abyssal needs to achieve before they can become some Deathlord like being. It'll be because they master necromancy, found thier own dread empire or kill their boss and take thier shit instead.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T19:29:50-08:00","id":843749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/843641-2e-infernals-3e-abyssals?p=843713#post843713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't those just be custom (and possibly esoteric) Abyssal charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T21:12:32-08:00","id":843799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/843641-2e-infernals-3e-abyssals#post843641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you guys think that Abyssals will be able to fashion themselves into custom Deathlords the same way Infernals made themselves into Devil-Tigers? Or would that be too samey?</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't so much that it would be too samey as that &quot;transhumanism&quot; has never really been part of the Abyssal design space.<br /> <br /> I mean, I'm sure something like that is probably <i>possible</i>. But there likely won't be a lot of support for it. An Abyssal who wants to wield ultimate power over death already has a tool for doing so that surpasses whatever unholy might the Deathlords were imbued with at their inception and managed to acquire over the centuries, and that tool is <i>themselves</i> and their Black Exaltation. In time, the Abyssals will likely surpass their masters.<br /> <br /> There are reasons for eschewing that, like if you get someone who is really into the whole Oblivion thing and decides that being an Abyssal is still too close to being alive. But like I said, probably not a ton of support there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T03:06:14-08:00","id":843871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/843641-2e-infernals-3e-abyssals?p=843710#post843710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mean actually BECOMING a Deathlord, but rather creating charms based on your own interpretation of the void's deathly essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the way it will play out in the books will be very reminiscent of what is familiar to us from Second Edition, let alone that the Deathlords will be as evident in the Abyssal Charms as some people are assuming they are.<br /> <br /> I mean, in the backer preview, you have those Presence Charms that feel a lot like they were inspired by the Lover, and yet many of them seem to match up surprisingly closely to the Solar Presence Charms. Even if the preview Charms were provisional, that suggests to me that there's a lot of room to make the whole thing very subtle.<br /> <br /> Besides, exactly how much room is there to interpret death? It's not a narrow concept to be sure, but I don't think it quite has the latitude that a lot of people drew on for Infernals.<br /> <br /> Even with all of that in mind, it wouldn't be something I would want. I like a bit of focus in the Exalted, and this seems like the kind of thing that creates or encourages dilution.<br /> <br /> I also personally dislike any sense that there are so many opportunities to develop the weird that the conventional becomes crowded out and forgotten, and the weird starts to feel either overwrought or desperate. It's like Martial Arts; there are reasons to not want a constant stream of weird, esoteric ones that leave things like being based off an animal buried.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T08:20:15-08:00","id":843970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/843641-2e-infernals-3e-abyssals?p=843799#post843799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It isn't so much that it would be too samey as that &quot;transhumanism&quot; has never really been part of the Abyssal design space.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is that transhumanist?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, exactly how much room is there to interpret death? It's not a narrow concept to be sure, but I don't think it quite has the latitude that a lot of people drew on for Infernals. </div> </div> </div>Well... Maybe I didn't word that properly. Okay. We have, for example, the vampiric succubus in the Lover, the undead necromancer in the mask, and so on. Each Deathlord covers a different type of &quot;undead overlord&quot;. Shouldn't there be room for other types as well? What about... the shepherd? Or the judge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T09:00:17-08:00","id":843991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/843641-2e-infernals-3e-abyssals?p=843970#post843970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is that transhumanist?<br /> <br /> <br /> Well... Maybe I didn't word that properly. Okay. We have, for example, the vampiric succubus in the Lover, the undead necromancer in the mask, and so on. Each Deathlord covers a different type of &quot;undead overlord&quot;. Shouldn't there be room for other types as well? What about... the shepherd? Or the judge?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the bishop covers those last two...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T09:11:02-08:00","id":843997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/843641-2e-infernals-3e-abyssals?p=843710#post843710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mean actually BECOMING a Deathlord, but rather creating charms based on your own interpretation of the void's deathly essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Custom Abyssal charms may have some of the trappings of Deathlords just like canon high-ESS Abyssal Charms will, but that need not be a requirement I'd think.<br /> <br /> As for Devil Tigers, I am thankful those things are gone from the game, so no, I doubt abyssals will do anything like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T10:19:18-08:00","id":844035,"title":"","content":"I don't think Abyssals need to do anything in particular to exemplify different aspects of death, as that's already well within their thematic space.<br /> <br /> Also, as far as I can glimpse the design intent behind tying Abyssal Charms to Deathlords, it's meant to emulate them about as much as Solar Charms emulate the Unconquered Sun - which is nothing like 2e Infernals not so much emulate, but literally embody the Yozis. It's just meant to give the writers a bit of solidity and personality behind the themes that were already part of the Abyssal shtick, but got glossed over or straight up ignored in favor of &quot;moar murder... and Solar mirrors!&quot; It's not some fundamental paradigm shift that's gonna end with Abyssals turning into Incarnae know what. They're still Underworld's Lawgivers, champions of the dead wielding the power of the Solar Exaltation tainted with death - it's just that, as Solar Charms' VFX draw on the visuals and themes of the UCS, Abyssal VFX will draw on the Deathlords' visuals and themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T10:22:57-08:00","id":844036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/843641-2e-infernals-3e-abyssals?p=843970#post843970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... Maybe I didn't word that properly. Okay. We have, for example, the vampiric succubus in the Lover, the undead necromancer in the mask, and so on. Each Deathlord covers a different type of &quot;undead overlord&quot;. Shouldn't there be room for other types as well? What about... the shepherd? Or the judge?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a point about how a number of Deathlords never even get detailed, but I suppose that's not really helpful here...<br /> <br /> When it comes to developing one's own stuff, I imagine it won't be very difficult to come up with Abyssal pinnacle concepts that fit the general champion of death thing as given precedent and structure by the Charms we're ultimately given and, implicitly, the Deathlords. I just don't think it would amount to much of an in-character or discretely mechanical <i>thing</i> in the way that the Heresy Charms did. I don't think it's necessary to imply that developing one's character or homebrew necessitates reinventing the wheel constantly, the way people really got over for the Heresy Charms, and started wanting for everything from Lunars to the Solars themselves.<br /> <br /> When we got comparisons between the Deathlords in Abyssal Charms and the actual Unconquered Sun for the Solars, I feel as though the whole thing is more about giving a coherent and expansive idea for what an Abyssal is and what they can do, which was a bit thin on the ground previously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T11:43:07-08:00","id":844076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/843641-2e-infernals-3e-abyssals?p=843727#post843727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think ... that Deathlords are ... ghetto ghost akuma</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/843641-2e-infernals-3e-abyssals?p=843727#post843727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>ghetto</b> ghost akuma</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T11:54:53-08:00","id":844081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/843641-2e-infernals-3e-abyssals?p=844076#post844076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note I'm mostly saying that in 3e, they probably <i>won't</i> be this. Which is all the better.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}